 "statistics_notes": [
  "Province wealth, tax base, goods output and recruit pool collapse into one stored `prosperity` value plus terrain/good weights: separate stored values would let events desync them and add clicks without decisions.",
  "Loyalty, autonomy, local governance, colonial control and territorial control are one `control` value; colonial_status says why control is low.",
  "Stability and legitimacy are kept separate because events need both: a legitimate dynasty can be unstable in a famine, and an illegitimate usurper can rule a stable realm.",
  "Morale, readiness and discipline collapse into derived military_quality.",
  "Disease exposure and public health share one stored value (province disease_burden) and one derived value (country public_health).",
  "Education, literacy and scientific development share `literacy`; applied science lives in tech_economy.",
  "Food production and food security are derived only; storing them would let events desync them from devastation and climate.",
  "Language is folded into culture.",
  "Exports and imports are not stored; trade_power and resource_dependency give the decisions they would support.",
  "Enslavement is never a trade good or a positive production modifier on the victims' land; it is modelled as forced population movement (move_population) with costs on the source societies and gains for the enslaving and plantation economies (see modifiers slave_trade_*)."
 ],
 "rebel_size_stat": "manpower_yield",
 "ai_factor_rules": {
  "$comment": "The numbers in balance.yaml ai_factors' descriptions.",
  "high_unrest_above": 50,
  "great_power_top": 8,
  "threatened_ratio": 1.5,
  "low_treasury_years_of_expenses": 1
 },
